# RANCO — FUNCTIONAL & NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Ranco is a real-time marketplace platform that connects people who need services with independent workers and professionals nearby.

The application must support both clients and professionals within the same account.

---

# CORE BUSINESS IDEA

Users can publish service requests such as:

- Plumbing
- Painting
- Cleaning
- Electrical repairs
- Babysitting
- Cooking
- Delivery
- Mechanical assistance
- Home repairs
- Pet care
- Tutoring
- Any informal or local service

Professionals can discover nearby opportunities and send offers to clients.

The platform must focus on:

- Trust
- Reputation
- Real-time interaction
- Fast hiring
- Local proximity
- Service reliability

---

# USER TYPES

The system must support:

## Client
A user who requests services.

## Professional
A user who offers services.

## Hybrid User
A user who can act as both client and professional.

Users must be able to switch modes dynamically inside the app.

---

# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

## Authentication

The app must allow users to:

- Register accounts
- Log in
- Recover passwords
- Maintain active sessions
- Log out securely

---

# Onboarding

After registration, users must be able to:

- Complete profile information
- Upload profile photo
- Choose whether they want to:
  - Request services
  - Offer services
  - Both

---

# User Profile

Users must be able to:

- Edit personal information
- Upload profile pictures
- Change contact information
- Configure notification preferences
- View ratings and reviews
- View service history

---

# Professional Profiles

Professionals must be able to:

- Add skills
- Select service categories
- Define service radius
- Configure availability
- Upload portfolio images
- Add work experience
- Set pricing references
- Enable or disable availability status

---

# Service Requests

Clients must be able to:

- Create service requests
- Add descriptions
- Add photos
- Select service categories
- Set urgency levels
- Choose location
- Publish requests
- Cancel requests
- View request status

---

# Discovery System

Professionals must be able to:

- Discover nearby requests
- Filter opportunities
- Search by category
- Search by distance
- Search by urgency

---

# Offer System

Professionals must be able to:

- Send offers to service requests
- Add messages to offers
- Suggest prices
- Withdraw offers

Clients must be able to:

- Receive offers
- Accept offers
- Reject offers
- Compare professionals

---

# Real-Time Chat

The app must support:

- Real-time messaging
- Message delivery states
- Read receipts
- Typing indicators
- Media sharing
- Chat history

---

# Notifications

Users must receive notifications for:

- New offers
- Accepted offers
- New messages
- Job status updates
- Ratings and reviews
- Nearby opportunities

---

# Job Lifecycle

The system must support service lifecycle states such as:

- Published
- In negotiation
- Accepted
- In progress
- Completed
- Cancelled

---

# Ratings & Reputation

Clients and professionals must be able to:

- Rate each other
- Leave reviews
- Build reputation scores
- View public ratings

The system should prioritize trust and reliability.

---

# Geolocation Features

The app must support:

- User location detection
- Nearby professionals
- Nearby service requests
- Distance-based discovery
- Location selection on map

---

# Presence System

The system must support:

- Online/offline status
- Availability indicators
- Active professionals nearby

---

# Media Features

Users must be able to:

- Upload profile photos
- Upload job images
- Upload portfolio media
- Share images in chat

---

# Search & Filtering

Users must be able to filter by:

- Category
- Distance
- Rating
- Availability
- Price range
- Urgency

---

# History

Users must be able to:

- View completed jobs
- View cancelled jobs
- View previous chats
- View transaction history
- View reviews history

---

# Future-Ready Features

The system structure must allow future implementation of:

- Payments
- Wallets
- Identity verification
- Background checks
- Escrow systems
- Subscription plans
- AI recommendations
- Dynamic pricing
- Multi-language support
- Multi-country support

---

# NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

## Scalability

The application must support future growth in:

- Users
- Messages
- Service requests
- Real-time events
- Media uploads

---

# Performance

The app must feel:

- Fast
- Responsive
- Smooth
- Real-time

Navigation and interactions should minimize delays.

---

# Reliability

The system must handle:

- Intermittent internet connections
- Real-time reconnections
- Failed uploads
- Notification retries

---

# Security

The system must protect:

- User data
- Chats
- Media
- Account access
- Personal information

Users should only access authorized data.

---

# Maintainability

The codebase must be:

- Modular
- Organized
- Extensible
- Easy to maintain
- Easy to scale

---

# Reusability

The application must maximize reuse of:

- Components
- Logic
- Validation
- Business rules

---

# Accessibility

The app should support:

- Readable interfaces
- Proper touch targets
- Accessible navigation
- Clear visual hierarchy

---

# Offline Tolerance

The app should gracefully handle:

- Slow internet
- Temporary disconnections
- Reconnection flows

---

# Real-Time Responsiveness

Real-time events should update the UI immediately for:

- Messages
- Offers
- Status changes
- Presence updates
- Notifications

---

# UX EXPECTATIONS

The experience should feel:

- Modern
- Minimal
- Trustworthy
- Fast
- Fluid
- Human
- Local-first
- Community-driven

The app should prioritize simplicity and reduce friction between clients and professionals.

---

# MVP PRIORITIES

Prioritize implementation of:

1. Authentication
2. Profiles
3. Service requests
4. Offers
5. Real-time chat
6. Notifications
7. Geolocation
8. Reputation system

All other features can remain extensible for future versions.